1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Hello everyone, today we are going to learn how to use the selection grid tool to deal with the problem of clothes passing through the model.

2
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Since we are going to use the selection grid tool, let's first learn about its basic knowledge.

3
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Select the mouse and select the grid brush tool.

4
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
In the drop-down menu, you can see three selection grid tools that can be used.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,000
The first is the selection grid brush.

6
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Use this tool to press the mouse and left keys on the board and drag and drop to highlight the selected area.

7
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
There are various additional functions that can be used on the right key in the selected area.

8
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:51,000
For example, the selected part of the grid is divided into details and the selected area is converted into a fixed frame.

9
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Or you can move it around or shape it.

10
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Among them, the part of the grid is converted into a fixed frame and the part of the grid is frozen, which is related to soft selection.

11
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:02,000
The darker the selected area is, the stronger the application effect is.

12
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:06,000
In the brush setting, the strength of the brush is the strength of the brush in the painting process.

13
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,000
The higher the number, the stronger the selection area effect.

14
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:15,000
On the other hand, the lower the strength, the softer the application effect.

15
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,000
The size is the size of the area selected by the brush.

16
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:23,000
The focus is on the center of the brush.

17
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:25,000
The center of the brush is completely applied.

18
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,000
The size of the area is not reduced.

19
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:30,000
When the focus value is high, the reduction area is very small.

20
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Most of them are completely applied to the set strength value.

21
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:36,000
The smaller the focus value, the more the reduction part.

22
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:41,000
It should be noted that the selection grid brush function is not able to move or rotate the grid.

23
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:46,000
So its function is to select the grid and then use the right keys.

24
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Now let's take a look at the selection grid comparison function.

25
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Use the selection grid comparison function.

26
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:58,000
In the 3D window, hold down the left mouse button and drag the mouse to select the grid that needs to be modified.

27
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:05,000
The selected area will be highlighted in green and will be highlighted in the same way in the 2D and 3D windows.

28
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Similarly, we can use this tool to select the grid top in the 2D window.

29
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Click on the 2D or 3D background to cancel the selection grid.

30
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Click on the grid top to select only one grid top.

31
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Click on the grid top on the line to select the entire line.

32
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Double-click on the grid in the version and select the grid top of the entire version.

33
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:36,000
When choosing a section, if you select another section directly, the selection will be cancelled.

34
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:43,000
If we need to select several grid top of the area at the same time,

35
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:50,000
then we need to hold down the CTRL and SHIFT keys to stop selecting and then select all the grid top.

36
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,000
The grid top that needs to be selected is selected.

37
00:02:52,000 --> 00:03:06,000
If you only press Shift and continue to select the grid, then the selected grid will be canceled, and the unselected grid will be selected.

38
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:17,000
If you only press Ctrl and continue to select, then the selected grid will be canceled.

39
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:21,000
After selecting, click on the selected grid.

40
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:33,000
You can move or rotate the selected area by positioning the ball.

41
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Note that the center of rotation is where you click when selecting the grid.

42
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:54,000
After adjusting the grid position, turn on the simulation.

43
00:03:54,000 --> 00:04:01,000
The board will reset the simulation and return to the correct simulation position.

44
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:05,000
When using the Select Grid Comparison or Select Grid Search function,

45
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:08,000
right-click on the grid in the selected area.

46
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,000
There is an option to rotate the grid level.

47
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:15,000
After selecting this option, the selected grid will automatically rotate the level.

48
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,000
If you select the grid,

49
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,000
the grid will rotate vertically,

50
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,000
and the grid will rotate vertically.

51
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:25,000
These functions are used to quickly adjust the grid position.

52
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:31,000
Grid rotation is mainly used to deal with the problem of grid surface damage or the back of the grid.

53
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,000
Here we will learn about the deep-layer fixing pin.

54
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:37,000
If the selected grid area is converted into a fixing pin,

55
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
then after we open the simulation,

56
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:42,000
this area will not return to its original position.

57
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:45,000
They will be fixed in the 3D space.

58
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Right-click on the fixing pin area,

59
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,000
we can delete the extra fixing pins.

60
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:53,000
We will talk about the other functions in other tutorial videos.

61
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:55,000
There is not much to talk about here.

62
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:58,000
Finally, I will briefly introduce the Select Grid Comparison function.

63
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:03,000
The difference between this tool and the Select Grid Comparison tool is only in the method of selecting the grid.

64
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:08,000
The Select Grid Comparison tool is to use a mouse to draw a locking area,

65
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:11,000
and then select the grid peak in the area.

66
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:15,000
Now let's see how to use the Select Grid tool to deal with the problem of hand insertion.

67
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:22,000
In the process of using the Select Grid tool to select the grid peak and adjust it,

68
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:27,000
we can only select the grid that can be seen in the current view.

69
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:33,000
If the grid in the area is blocked by other objects in the 3D space,

70
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,000
such as a virtual model,

71
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,000
or by other panels,

72
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,000
or in a position that cannot be seen in our view,

73
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:43,000
then there is no way to be selected at the same time.

74
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:45,000
Therefore, in the process of selection,

75
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,000
we can select the grid in the 3D space first,

76
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:50,000
and then refer to the position of the green height.

77
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:55,000
In the 2D window, select the grid that needs to be modified in the frame,

78
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:59,000
and then move it back to the 3D window.

79
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:03,000
This can avoid the problem of the invisible grid being unable to be selected.

80
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:06,000
Next, we will repeat the previous operation.

81
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:10,000
After selecting the grid in the 2D window,

82
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:12,000
go back to the 3D window, use the positioning ball,

83
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,000
and pull these grid out a little,

84
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:17,000
so that they do not intersect with the hand.

85
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:20,000
Then there are some repeated operations.

86
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:22,000
We can adjust them in large pieces first,

87
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:25,000
and then adjust them in small parts.

88
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,000
Then turn on the simulation,

89
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:46,000
wait for the panel to slowly simulate the original position.

90
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:54,000
After the simulation is complete,

91
00:06:54,000 --> 00:07:01,000
we will continue to select the grid in the 2D window,

92
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:04,000
and then move them to the 3D space.

93
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:13,000
Next, let's take a look at how to adjust the other side.

94
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:17,000
On the other side, the entire sleeve panel is outside.

95
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:20,000
What we have to do is to lift the sleeve up first,

96
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:23,000
so that the sleeve panel can be aligned with the position of the wrist.

97
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:30,000
When the sleeve panel is almost aligned with the position of the wrist,

98
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:32,000
we will pause the simulation,

99
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:34,000
and then we will start to select the grid.

100
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,000
Here it is still the same,

101
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:37,000
we select it in the 3D space,

102
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:39,000
and then in the 2D space,

103
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:42,000
use the position of the height just now as a reference to select the grid,

104
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,000
and then go back to the 3D space,

105
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,000
let the grid pass through the wrist,

106
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:50,000
and pull out some of the other holes.

107
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:53,000
Then press the control button to start the simulation,

108
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:55,000
and wait for the simulation to stabilize.

109
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,000
If there are still some gaps,

110
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:00,000
then continue to repeat the previous operation.

111
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:08,000
Finally, if the positioning ball you use is different from the coordinate system used in my video,

112
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:11,000
it may be that you used a default screen coordinate.

113
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:14,000
Right-click in the 3D background,

114
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:15,000
select the positioning ball,

115
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:17,000
you can select the world coordinate,

116
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,000
so it's the same as me,

117
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,000
it's based on the world as a coordinate.

118
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:23,000
Because the default screen coordinate is based on the camera,

119
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,000
so it's based on the 3D view.

120
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,000
See you next time.

121
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:27,000
Bye bye.

